## SOFT CELL - TAINTED LOVE
#  Full Arrangement Cover for PULP / SKRED. 144 BPM, G minor, 105 bars (~2:55).
#  Written by Ed Cobb (1964), Produced by Mike Thorne, Performed by Soft Cell (1981).
#  Self-contained: drums from built-in waves 82-99, Prophet-5 synth hook stabs,
#  Korg Synthe-Bass, octave synth comp, Synclavier bells, Marc Almond vocal lead.
#  Zero synthetic noise risers - dynamic builds driven by authentic 1981 synthpop.
#  All patterns strictly pinned to exact bar boundaries (x15, x31, x63, x127).
#  Load:   [tainted_love.sk] /ls
#  Start:  play        Stop:  stop
#
#  VOICE MAP (all labeled via [name] vt):
#    v0  four-on-the-floor kick (w82) + v5 sub punch (w0)
#    v1  CR-78 crisp gated snare (w83) + v4 electronic clap (w86)
#    v2  closed hat 8ths/16ths (w84)  v3  open hat offbeat (w85)
#    v17 crash cymbal (w94)  v18 hi tom (w90)  v19 mid tom (w91)
#    v11 main synth stab root (w15) + v12 5th (w15) + v13 oct (w16) -> Bus 1
#    v6  Korg Synthe-Bass low saw (w1) + v7 sub pulse oct (w2)
#    v21 octave synth comp low (w15)  v22 comp high (w16) -> Bus 3
#    v15 Synclavier bell lead (w10) + v16 chime (w10)
#    v8  Marc Almond vocal lead (w15) + v9 (w15 left), v10 (w16 right) -> Bus 2
#    v14 Marc Almond backing vocal (w15) + v14 right
#
#  DELAY BUSES:
#    Bus 1: Delta Labs DL4 digital slapback / ping-pong for synth stabs (16th)
#    Bus 2: Marc Almond vocal hall space echo (dotted eighth, 144 BPM)
#    Bus 3: Synclavier octave comp & bell reverb wash (quarter note)
#    Bus 4: Snare & electronic clap gated room tail (eighth note)
#
#  ARRANGEMENT (105 bars):
#    0-3   Intro: Solo Prophet-5 synth stab hook + closed hats
#    4-7   Korg Synthe-Bass enters with octave comp and full beat
#    8-23  Verse 1: Full groove, kick, snare, claps, Marc's vocal
#    24-35 Chorus 1: G-major lift, 'Once I ran to you...', D-major tension
#    36-39 Interlude: Riff vamp + Synclavier bell hook ('Tainted love!')
#    40-55 Verse 2: 'Now I know I've got to run away...', full driving beat
#    56-67 Chorus 2: High vocal passion, bell arpeggios, dominant turnaround
#    68-79 Bridge: Drums drop to kick pulse, tense breakdown ('Don't touch me...')
#    80-91 Chorus 3: Climax wall of sound, full emotional release
#    92-103 Outro Vamp: Extended club groove, Marc's ad-libs, cascading bells
#    104   Hard cold end on beat 1, solo synth stab delay tail into silence
# ======================================================================

[TAINTED LOVE - SOFT CELL] puts
M 144 16

## DELAY BUSES
# Bus 1: Delta Labs DL4 digital slapback / ping-pong for Synth Hook Stabs (16th note)
DS 1 144 .25
DL 1 - - 4 0 0 8
DD 1 7 2
DP 1 1

# Bus 2: Marc Almond vocal hall space echo (dotted eighth)
DS 2 144 .75
DL 2 - - 8 2 3 11
DD 2 6 3
DP 2 1

# Bus 3: Synclavier octave comp & bell reverb wash (quarter note)
DS 3 144 1
DL 3 - - 10 3 6 12
DD 3 7 3

# Bus 4: Snare & electronic clap gated room tail (eighth note)
DS 4 144 .5
DL 4 - - 6 0 0 8
DD 4 5 4

## VOICES
# Drums: Roland CR-78 style punchy kick + sub
v0 w82 f440 a7 p0 [kick electronic] vt
v5 w0 a-2 p0 t.001,.20,0,.05 j1 k180 q.7 [kick sub punch] vt

# Crisp snare, claps, hats, crash, toms
v1 w83 f440 a8 p0 r3 ds.20 [snare cr78 gated] vt
v2 w84 f440 a-3 p.25 [closed hat] vt
v3 w85 f440 a-2 p-.25 [open hat] vt
v4 w86 f440 a7 p0 ds.20 [electronic clap] vt
v17 w94 f440 a4 p.2 [crash cymbal] vt
v18 w90 f480 a6 p-.3 [electronic hi tom] vt
v19 w91 f380 a6 p.3 [electronic mid tom] vt

# The REAL Iconic Main Synth Stab Hook (Prophet-5 G-D-G power chord)
# Warm analog brass punch on beats 1 and 2, and upbeat 2-and and beat 4
v11 w15 a2 p-.25 t.005,.32,.25,.18 j1,2 k2200 q2.2 r1 ds.25 [synth stab root] vt
v11 >12
v11 >13
v12 w15 a0 N0,7 p.25 t.005,.32,.25,.18 j1,2 k2200 q2.2 r1 ds.25 [synth stab 5th] vt
v13 w16 a-2 N0,12 p0 r0 ds.20 [synth stab oct] vt
v11 G12,13 H12,13

# Dave Ball's Korg Synthe-Bass (G1-Bb1-Eb1-C1 with sub octave pulse)
v6 w1 a4 p-.1 t.002,.26,.30,.12 j1 k1400 q2.8 r2 ds.08 [korg bass low] vt
v6 >7
v7 w2 a0 N0,12 p.25 r0 [korg bass oct] vt
v6 G7 H7

# Octave Synth Comp (doubles the bass ostinato in upper octaves)
v21 w15 a-4 p-.35 t.003,.24,.20,.10 j1 k2400 q1.8 ds.15 [octave synth low] vt
v22 w16 a-4 p.35 t.003,.24,.20,.10 j1 k2400 q1.8 ds.15 [octave synth high] vt

# Analog Warm Counter-Melody
v15 w15 a-8 p-.25 t.005,.35,.20,.15 j1 k2400 q1.5 ds.25 [analog counter melody] vt
v15 >16
v16 w16 a-10 N0,12 p.4 r0 ds.20 [analog counter partner] vt
v15 G16 H16

# Marc Almond Vocal Lead: expressive, theatrical, soulful singing synth
# Smooth singing sustain and release
v8 w15 a-2 p0 t.02,.60,.35,.20 j1 k2400 q1.2 g.08 c4,.20 r1 ds.35 P18 [marc almond lead] vt
v8 >9
v8 >10
v9 w15 a-6 N0,8 p-.45 r0 [marc vocal left] vt
v10 w16 a-7 N0,-8 p.45 r0 [marc vocal right] vt
v8 G9,10 H9,10

# Marc Almond Backing Vocal / Shouts
v14 w15 a-5 p-.3 t.02,.9,0,.15 j1 k3000 q1.5 ds.30 P12 [marc backing shout] vt

